From 8e21548835b5e165215b54c3288a1d9c7d89a983 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dennis Wuitz <dennish@wuitz.de>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 14:56:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] libexpr: let the embedder fetch

An embedder that evaluates on many machines wants one place that
fetches, caches and rate-limits downloads, instead of every evaluator
fetching for itself. fetchers::Settings::fetchHook replaces the
built-in fetchers when set: it receives the request as JSON, with the
builtin, its arguments and the expected store path when the input is
locked, and answers with the store path it made valid and, for
fetchTree, the locked attributes. The hook is not consulted for inputs
already in the store or for the path scheme.

nix_eval_state_builder_set_fetch_hook() installs a C callback as the
hook.
---
